module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.generic_coproduct_argument_unjudged_at_declared_return

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data generic_coproduct_argument_unjudged_at_declared_return: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "generic_coproduct_argument_unjudged_at_declared_return" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a fn declared to return one instantiation of a generic coproduct (`Outcome<Node>`) was admitted while its body produced another (`Outcome<ResolvedTree record>`).** DESIGN section 4b puts `values inhabit declared types` on the ordinary compiler floor, so this is below the floor, not a rung. Found by `wise-bat-862` in gunbc#12432, where about 35 test helpers carried the mismatch and nothing refused.",

    "THE CHAIN, per DESIGN section 6b. `v1.compiler.infer` `declared_type_conformance_diags` is the one judgment the declared-return and data-initializer positions consult. Its arms are: ground kernels and one-peel element collections; `nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal`, which compares applied type arguments through `applied_type_arguments_conflict` but abstains on any head that is not a declared PRODUCT; `coproduct_payload_where_parent_required`, which excludes generic coproducts by its own contract; the callable arms; and a terminal `!both_ground => []`. An application of a generic coproduct matches no judging arm, and it is never ground, so it reaches the terminal arm and is admitted by fallthrough. The arguments were never dropped by a comparison; no arm existed to compare them. The product arm's own note had filed this as the separate generic half of the inhabitance defect.",

    "REPAIR: `nominal_coproduct_applied_argument_conflict`, a sibling arm that consumes the two authorities the product arm already uses: `nominal_product_head_names_agree` for constructor identity and `applied_type_arguments_conflict` for the fail-open per-argument relation, where a type variable, an optional, a callable or a nested application is never read as a disagreement. It refuses only two applications of ONE declared coproduct constructor whose resolved arguments are both established and differ. RED (both directions) and positive control: `test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness` `w_a_wrong_argument_of_a_two_arm_coproduct_at_a_declared_return_is_refused` and `w_a_matching_or_type_variable_argument_of_a_two_arm_coproduct_is_admitted`, beside the six single-arm rows enrolled red in `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red` chunk 24; which of those this arm greens is measured on the regenerated seed, and each greened row leaves the roster.",

    "REVERSE-DIRECTION SPECIMEN (reported by `wise-bat-862`, gunbc#12432, CI run 36341040827): `pick_ingested_arrow_from_source` briefly declared `-> Outcome<ResolvedTree>` while its body returned `Outcome<Node>`. It typechecked and failed only at runtime with `no field root on type Node`. So both directions were admitted, record-over-Node and Node-over-record. The four helpers in #12432 that still return `Outcome<Node>` / `Optional<Node>` (`ingested_arrow_from_source` and its twin, `pick_ingested_arrow_from_source`, `infer_transform_witness_resolved_add_arrow`, `pbf_resolved_add_arrow`) do so deliberately: they return an extracted arrow node, not the record.",

    "MEASURED ON THE REGENERATED SEED (srv1, `neat-boar-16`, head 3689f2b48ce against merge-base e66a6a65ae5; the instrument is the whole-corpus covering compile differential named in `declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel`). Witness: of the six single-arm rows enrolled red in `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red` chunk 24, the four same-head argument rows (positions zero, one, two, and carried in a field) PASSED and leave the roster; `w_a_different_application_head_at_a_declared_return_is_refused` and `w_a_wrong_nested_type_argument_at_a_declared_return_is_refused` stay red, outside this arm by construction (it requires one constructor, and fails open on a nested argument). Corpus: 181 to 186 blocking, 5 newly refused, 0 no longer refused, and ALL FIVE WERE FALSE: `gunbc.fleet.app_control_plane_inspection` `assess_registration`, `test.claim.goal_assessment_witness_test` `fixture_assess`, `test.claim.realization_selection_witness_test` `selection_assess`, `v2.compiler.target_carriers` `fidelity_disposition_node_decode_fidelity`, `v2.compiler.wrap_decision` `wrap_decision_gate`. Each had Unit (or an empty name) in the PRODUCED argument vector where a generic call site had no evidence for that parameter -- `outcome_accepted(Lossless)` read as Outcome<Unit>. The repair was fixed at its own arm, not by exemption: a produced Unit argument is not an established identity there, judged per argument, following `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch`'s existing exit on an actual named Unit. Positive control: `w_an_unsolved_argument_of_a_two_arm_coproduct_call_is_admitted`.",

    "THE UPSTREAM DEFECT THAT FORCED THAT NARROWING IS ITS OWN BELOW-FLOOR CLASS and is not repaired here: the v1 seed's call-site generic solve answers Unit for a type parameter it did not solve, even where the declared return (the expected type) determines it. Unit is a real type, so the solve fabricates an identity rather than reporting absence, and every judgment downstream must either special-case Unit or refuse correct code. That Unit is a FABRICATED DEFAULT, the absorbing-fallback shape of DESIGN section 5, and this arm's Unit exit inherits it: a genuinely Unit-typed argument against a different declared argument is admitted. The limitation is bounded and enrolled red rather than silent: `test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness` `w_a_genuine_unit_argument_of_a_two_arm_coproduct_at_a_declared_return_is_refused`, in `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red` chunk 24.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silently admitted). RUNG AFTER REPAIR: structurally guaranteed for a single-level argument of a declared generic coproduct at the declared-return and data-initializer positions of the v1 seed. CEILING: structurally guaranteed (a wrong return is authorable in source). NOT COVERED, stated rather than implied: nested application arguments (`Outcome<List<A>>` against `Outcome<List<B>>`), optional and callable arguments, and early `return` exits only as far as they already route through the same judgment. v2 has the same class in a wider form: `v2.std.inhabitance` `PositionDeclaredReturn` is declared, but no `DeclaredTypeObligation` producer in `v2.compiler.infer` emits it, so v2 judges no declared return at all. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, NAMED AS CAPABILITIES. FIRST: v1 call-site generic solving answers an unsolved type parameter as an explicit UNSOLVED rather than as Unit, sufficient for this arm to delete its Unit exit and for the genuine-Unit row to leave the roster. SECOND: one inhabitance judgment that recurses over applied type arguments of ANY established head (product, coproduct, nested application), sufficient to delete both head-kind-keyed argument arms, AND a v2 declared-return obligation producer consulting it.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
